="journal">Godfrey, D.I., K.J. Hammond, L.D. Poulton, M.J. Smyth, and A.G. Baxter. <year>2000</year>. NKT cells: facts, functions and fallacies. <source>Immunol. Today.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>573</fpage>&#x02013;583.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11094262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kronenberg, M., and L. Gapin. <year>2002</year>. The unconventional lifestyle of NKT cells. <source>Nat. Rev. Immunol.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>557</fpage>&#x02013;568.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12154375</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gumperz, J.E., C. Roy, A. Makowska, D. Lum, M. Sugita, T. Podrebarac, Y. Koezuka, S.A. Porcelli, S. Cardell, M.B. Brenner, and S.M. Behar. <year>2000</year>. Murine CD1d-restricted T cell recognition of cellular lipids. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>211</fpage>&#x02013;221.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10714687</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wu, D.Y., N.H. Segal, S. Sidobre, M. Kronenberg, and P.B. Chapman. <year>2003</year>. Cross-presentation of disialoganglioside GD3 to natural killer T cells. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>198</volume>:<fpage>173</fpage>&#x02013;181.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12847141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Shamshiev, A., H.J. Gober, A. Donda, Z. Mazorra, L. Mori, and G. De Libero. <year>2002</year>. Presentation of the same glycolipid by different CD1 molecules. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>195</volume>:<fpage>1013</fpage>&#x02013;1021.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11956292</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Steinman, L. <year>1996</year>. Multiple sclerosis: a coordinated immunological attack against myelin in the central nervous system. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>85</volu